# `.ai-state/observations.jsonl` is an append-only write-ahead log. Every
# worktree accumulates its own session's lines on top of a shared base, so a
# merge sees both sides having "modified" the same region and conflicts --
# every single time, on a file whose correct resolution is always the same:
# keep both sides. Git's built-in `union` driver does exactly that, and doing
# it automatically removes the one step of a worktree merge where a human
# under time pressure is most likely to resolve by picking a side and silently
# discarding another session's observations.
#
# Union is safe here precisely because the file is append-only and its records
# are independent: duplicate lines are idempotent to every reader, and no
# record's meaning depends on its neighbours. Do not extend this to a file
# where order or uniqueness carries meaning.
.ai-state/observations.jsonl merge=union

# Praxion semantic merge drivers — see rules/swe/agent-intermediate-documents.md
.ai-state/observations.jsonl merge=observations-jsonl
